message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "EXTRAI: an evidence-extraction benchmark for local LLMs (Brazilian Portuguese)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Barra"
    given-names: "Gustavo Barcelos"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2136-3471"
version: "1.2.0"
date-released: 2026-08-30
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22159050"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gbbarra/llm-evidence-extraction-benchmark-ptbr"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - local LLMs
  - evidence extraction
  - systematic review
  - meta-analysis
  - benchmark
  - risk of bias
  - Ollama
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  EXTRAI tests whether local LLMs (gemma4:12b/26b, qwen3:14b, qwen3.8:27b via
  Ollama, on consumer hardware) can redo the work of a published meta-analysis:
  cell-by-cell evidence extraction from all 14 of its randomized trials against
  a source-verified answer key (Study 1), and the meta-analytic arithmetic --
  risk ratios, confidence intervals, pooling -- by head versus through a
  text-protocol calculator (Study 2). Includes pre-registered protocols with
  dated amendments, a dual reading-proof by number perturbation, fully
  mechanical grading with public adjudication records, and errata files for
  the anchor meta-analysis and for the adjudicator himself. Sibling of the
  FIEL summarization benchmark.
